    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="0877" n="865" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/24: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-27T15:00:00+02:00">March 27, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 27—12:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>590. Department’s 444, March 26, 8 p.m. Having ascertained that Ibn Saud is at or
                    near Riyadh,<anchor n="61" xml:id="d901-f1"/> I propose to leave for Saudi
                    Arabia via Bahrein within a week’s time provided airplane travel can be
                    arranged. Hare<anchor n="62" xml:id="d901-f2"/> and Rountree will accompany
                    me.</p>
                <p>Am gratified that prospects of obtaining irrigation machinery for Saudi Arabia
                    are favorable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d901-f1" n="61" xml:id="d901-f1-content">
                <p>The capital of Saudi Arabia; the King spent only a week or ten days of each year,
                    during the pilgrimage season, at Jidda, location of the diplomatic
                    establishment.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d901-f2" n="62" xml:id="d901-f2-content">
                <p>Raymond A. Hare, Second Secretary of Legation in Egypt.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
